# Customer Onboarding Doctrine & Runbook (Frappe Cloud)

## Objective
Stand up a production-ready, agentic CRM for a new customer in hours with a repeatable, low-risk process.

## Environments
- Bench (shared per region) → Sites (one per customer) → Apps (`crm` from `fjkiani/crm-deployment`).
- Data and secrets are site-scoped.

## 1) Bench & App
1. Frappe Cloud → Bench (target) → Apps → Add App:
   - Repo: `fjkiani/crm-deployment`  • Branch: `main`  • Pull/Update
2. Confirm app structure per doctrine: packaging at repo root, app under `crm/`.
   - [pyproject.toml](mdc:pyproject.toml), [setup.py](mdc:setup.py), [MANIFEST.in](mdc:MANIFEST.in)

## 2) Site Provisioning
1. Create Site → Select Bench → Install Apps → choose `crm` → Continue.
2. After provision: Site → Actions → Migrate → Clear Cache → Restart.
3. Domains & SSL: attach custom domain if required.

## 3) Baseline Configuration (10–15 min)
- Masters (minimum viable):
  - CRM Lead Status: Open, Qualified, Won, Lost.
  - CRM Lead Source: Research, Inbound, Referral, Event.
- Branding: logo/letterhead; timezone; currency.
- Roles: System Manager, Sales, Support. Disable public signups.

## 4) Email (two paths)
### Fast Path (works today)
- Site → Email Account → IMAP/SMTP (app password) • "Always use Account’s Email Address as Sender" → Save • Send/Receive test.

### Scalable Path (Gmail OAuth)
- Tenant-wide client: Integrations → Google OAuth (client id/secret).
- Per-user connect: OAuth consent → choose backfill window.
- Polling now; Pub/Sub later per Gmail doctrine.

## 5) Data Import
### Built-in Data Import (per DocType)
1. Desk → Data Import → Import from Google Sheets/CSV.
2. Fix link fields by ensuring master values exist (e.g., Status, Source).
3. Validate → Import. Use the blank template to discover fields/links.

### Our ETL (multi-entity, reusable)
- Mapping Profile:
  - DocType: `CRM Import Column Map` → Actions → Auto‑generate Mapping (CSV/Sheets) → Save.
  - UI button is wired by [crm_import_column_map.js](mdc:crm/crm/fcrm/doctype/crm_import_column_map/crm_import_column_map.js).
- Import Job (API):
  - POST `/api/method/crm.api.etl.import_rows` with payload {title, source_type (CSV|GOOGLE_SHEETS), file_url|sheet_id, mapping_profile, dedupe:true, link_organization:true}.
  - Monitor `CRM Import Job` for Status/Counts; failures attach error CSV.
- Code refs: [etl.py](mdc:crm/crm/api/etl.py), [CRM Import Job](mdc:crm/crm/fcrm/doctype/crm_import_job/crm_import_job.json), [CRM Import Column Map](mdc:crm/crm/fcrm/doctype/crm_import_column_map/crm_import_column_map.json).
- Behavior: dedupe (Lead by email/phone; Org by website/name); normalizes Status/Source to Title Case; optional per-column transforms.

## 6) Telephony & WhatsApp (optional)
- Twilio: Integrations → Twilio • SID/Token • click‑to‑call + call logs ([twilio/api.py](mdc:crm/crm/integrations/twilio/api.py)).
- Exotel: handset flow via agent mobile.
- WhatsApp: add `frappe_whatsapp` on bench; configure provider; test in/outbound.

## 7) SPA & Navigation
- Primary UI: `/crm` SPA.
- Optional: add SPA link to Desk Data Import for non-technical users.

## 8) Observability, Backup, Safety
- Enable daily backups (DB + files). Verify restore.
- Monitor Error Log & Background Jobs; alerts on job failures.
- Private file storage for error CSVs; PII handling per policy.

## 9) Bootstrap Template (Repeatability)
- Keep a clean staging site with:
  - Masters preseeded (statuses/sources), default views, sample mapping.
  - Fixtures for masters & views to reuse across customers.
- Optionally add a `site_bootstrap.py` to seed masters + run ETL dry‑run on new sites.

## 10) Timeline & Roles
- T0: Site + app install; baseline masters; branding (SM).
- T0+0.5d: Email fast path; import test; first automations (SM/Owner).
- T0+1–2d: OAuth rollout, ETL schedule, telephony/WhatsApp (optional) (Admin).

## 11) Acceptance Criteria
- Email send/receive working; inbox visible.
- Leads imported; dedupe effective; orgs linked.
- At least one automation (follow‑up draft) verified.
- Backups scheduled; alerts configured.

## 12) Cutover & Rollback
- Cutover: freeze legacy; final delta import; user training; flip DNS.
- Rollback: restore backup; disable connectors; communicate plan.

